From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:33:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] qt: keep the video window within the screen's width too

MainInterface::setVideoSize() fitted the window to the screen only when the
video was too high. A video wider than the screen but not too high, such as a
3840x1080 side by side video on a 1920 wide output, opened a window twice as
wide as the screen, so only its left half was visible.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
---
 modules/gui/qt/main_interface.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules/gui/qt/main_interface.cpp b/modules/gui/qt/main_interface.cpp
index b90122f..26f7330 100644
--- a/modules/gui/qt/main_interface.cpp
+++ b/modules/gui/qt/main_interface.cpp
@@ -840,7 +840,8 @@ void MainInterface::setVideoSize( unsigned int w, unsigned int h )
 #else
             float factor = 1.0f;
 #endif
-            if( (float)h / factor > screen.height() )
+            if( (float)h / factor > screen.height()
+             || (float)w / factor > screen.width() )
             {
                 w = screen.width();
                 h = screen.height();
